{
  "slug": "records",
  "name": "Records",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Records is a local-first FHIR validation and data-quality workflow plugin for Claude Code. It helps FHIR developers, IG authors, and AI agents validate FHIR JSON, explain OperationOutcome issues, map generated SUSHI/FSH artifacts back to source, derive project quality rules, and add CI validation while preserving privacy boundaries. It uses local or user-configured runtimes first and does not send patient data to external services by default.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 skills**, **1 agent** and **5 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (3): `fhir-ci-quality` (Generate or review FHIR validator CI workflows and derive candidate healthcare data-quality rules from local FHIR examples), `fhir-project-doctor` (Inspect an HL7 FHIR, FSH/SUSHI, or Implementation Guide project for validator runtimes, FHIR package dependencies, cache state, version…), `fhir-validation` (Validate HL7 FHIR R4 JSON resources, FHIR profile and Implementation Guide examples, and AI-created FHIR output; explain OperationOutcome…)\n- **Agents** (1): `fhir-validation-reviewer` (Read-only reviewer for FHIR validation, IG, SUSHI/FSH, OperationOutcome, and Records setup issues)\n- **Commands** (5): `derive-quality-rules` (Derive reviewable FHIR data-quality rules from local project evidence), `doctor` (Diagnose the current repository's FHIR/IG validation setup with the Records fhir-validation skill), `explain-outcome` (Explain a FHIR OperationOutcome and separate safe fixes from domain/setup issues), `init-ci` (Add or update repository CI for Records FHIR validation), `validate` (Run end-to-end local FHIR validation with runtime planning, privacy gates, and structural fallback)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install records@claude-community` from `medvertical/claude-records` (`plugins/records`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
